// 1. $\beta \leftarrow 1 - 1/\max_c n_c$ (clipped at 0.9999); $E_c = (1-\beta^{n_c})/(1-\beta)$
// 2. $H_0 = -\sum p_c \log p_c$ with $p_c = n_c/\sum n_{c'}$;  $H_{\max} = \log C$
// 3. target $H_t = H_0 + r\,(H_{\max} - H_0)$,  $r = 0.55$ if $C\le 10$ else $0.50$
// 4. binary-search $\alpha \in [0, 2]$ for 64 iters:
// 5.   $w_c \leftarrow E_c^{-\alpha}$;  reweighted $p^\alpha_c \propto w_c n_c$
// 6.   if $H(p^\alpha) < H_t$ raise lower bound, else raise upper bound
// 7. weights $\leftarrow E^{-\alpha}$ normalised to sum $C$
